==English==

===Etymology===
{{etyl|xno}}, from {{etyl|fro}} ''tenement'', from {{etyl|ML.}} ''[[tenementum]]'', from {{etyl|la}} ''[[tenere]]''.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# a [[building]] that is [[rented]] to [[multiple]] [[tenant]]s, especially a low-rent, run-down one
# {{legal}} any form of [[property]] that is held by one person from another, rather than being owned

